values ('ap_chemistry', 8, '8.5', array['8.5']::text[], 'diagram', 'Titration curve (pH vs. volume of titrant)', 'A titration curve plots pH against the volume of titrant added and summarizes results from a titration; students read it to find the equivalence point and, for weak acids/bases, the half-equivalence point.', '[{"label": "Vertical axis", "meaning": "pH"}, {"label": "Horizontal axis", "meaning": "volume of titrant added"}, {"label": "Equivalence point", "meaning": "moles of titrant added equal moles of analyte originally present (monoprotic acids or bases); pH is set by the major species present (neutral for strong acid-strong base; basic for a weak acid titration, acidic for a weak base titration)"}, {"label": "Half-equivalence point", "meaning": "for a weak acid, the point halfway to the equivalence point where [HA] = [A−], so pH = pKa"}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'Do not confuse the half-equivalence point (pH = pKa) with the equivalence point; pKa is read from the pH at the half-equivalence point, not the equivalence point.', 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=task0067-chem-escalations-r3-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_chemistry-u8-r4-003; ced=8.5.A.1 A titration curve, plotting pH against the volume of titrant added; 8.5.A.3 half-equivalence point, pH = pKa')
